<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raden Wijaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1293">1293</a>–<a href="/years/1309">1309 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Wijaya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raden Wijaya was the founder and first ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, reigning from 1293 to 1309 CE. He used a Mongol expedition sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> to defeat his rivals, then turned against the Mongol forces and drove them out. His control of fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> lands and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java-sea">Java Sea</a> trade routes laid the foundations of Majapahit power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya.jpg" alt="Raden Wijaya" width="213" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harihara_Majapahit_1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Majapahit's founder <b>Raden Wijaya</b> used a Mongol army sent by Kublai Khan to defeat his rival, then turned on the invaders and drove them from Java.</blockquote><a href="/empire/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>…showed the limits of Mongol power in maritime and tropical environments: the Japanese expeditions were wrecked by storms, remembered in Japan as kamikaze or 'divine winds', while the Javanese expedition, after initial success, was outmanoeuvred by <b>Raden Wijaya</b>, founder of Majapahit, and forced to withdraw with significant losses.</blockquote><a href="/empire/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The throne passed within the house of <b>Raden Wijaya</b>, and a woman could hold it: when Jayanegara was murdered in 1328, childless, the Queen Grandmother Gayatri Rajapatni, who had become a Buddhist nun, set her daughter Tribhuwana on it.</blockquote><a href="/societies/majapahit">Social Hierarchy of Majapahit</a></li><li><blockquote>Majapahit forces under <b>Raden Wijaya</b>, who had used the Mongol expedition sent by Kublai Khan against his rival, turned on the invaders and won a major victory.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/may-31">31 May in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Raden Wijaya</b>, who had used a Mongol expedition sent by Kublai Khan to defeat his rivals and then driven the Mongol forces out, was crowned the first ruler of Majapahit in eastern Java, taking the name Kertarajasa Jayawardhana.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-10">10 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>He pardoned Kertanegara's son-in-law <b>Raden Wijaya</b>, who on the advice of Arya Wiraraja of Sumenep pretended submission and was given land at Tarik, where he founded Majapahit.</blockquote><a href="/state/gelang-gelang">Gelang-gelang</a></li></ul></section>
